<h2>Duplicate Properties</h2>
<p><strong>How Duplicate Properties Work on PropertyList.es</strong></p>
<p>Listing a property: each property entry includes details such as the property’s price, features, photos, etc. <a href="/docs/propertylist-mls-user-manual/listing-a-property/creating-a-new-listing/">Find out how to list a property here.</a></p>

<ol>
	<li><strong>Identifying duplicates:</strong> PropertyList uses various algorithms and human overview to identify potential duplicate listings by comparing photos, details and other relevant information.</li>
	<li><strong>Selecting the main listing:</strong> When duplicates are confirmed, the main listing is chosen based on a point system where the one with the best photos, most detailed information, overall completeness, first listing uploaded, if it is listed by a Verified Agency, and various other factors is prioritised.</li>
	<li><strong>Reporting duplicates:</strong> Agents can also report listings as duplicates. These reports are reviewed by PropertyList to verify and merge any duplicate entries.</li>
	<li><strong>MLS duplicate section:</strong> Other agents within the MLS can see all duplicate listings in a dedicated section of the main listing. This section includes the agency name, price, commission offered and a link to the property.</li>
	<li><strong>Maintaining accuracy:</strong> PropertyList continuously monitors listings to ensure accuracy and prevent future duplicates. Agents are encouraged to regularly update their listings to keep the information current.</li>
</ol>

<p>By following these steps, PropertyList maintains a clean and accurate database of properties, making it easier and more enjoyable for users to find the right property.</p>
