			desc: 'Manage enquiries from other agents inside the MLS.',
			body: `
<p data-sourcepos="3:1-3:201">PropertyList.es connects you with a valuable network. Gain access to leads from other agents within the MLS platform, allowing you to:</p><ul data-sourcepos="5:1-8:0"><li data-sourcepos="5:1-5:102"><strong>Tap into a wider pool of clients:</strong> Reach potential clients you might not have found on your own.</li><li data-sourcepos="6:1-6:105"><strong>Increase your deal flow:</strong> More leads mean more opportunities to close deals and grow your business.</li><li data-sourcepos="7:1-8:0"><strong>Collaborate with fellow agents:</strong> Connect with other professionals and build mutually beneficial relationships.</li></ul><p data-sourcepos="3:1-3:174">All leads from fellow agents within the MLS platform are conveniently delivered to the dedicated &#8220;<strong>MLS LEADS</strong>&#8221; tab in your account. Here, you can:</p><ul data-sourcepos="5:1-7:0"><li data-sourcepos="5:1-5:102"><strong>Clearly see all MLS leads:</strong> Easily access and review all incoming leads in one central location.</li><li data-sourcepos="6:1-7:0"><strong>Effortless lead assignment:</strong> Seamlessly assign leads to specific team members for efficient follow-up.</li></ul><h3>When an agent messages you about a specific property: (Check Availability)</h3><p><strong>1. Receive a New MLS Lead</strong></p><ul><li>When you receive a new MLS lead, you&#8217;ll see a notification indicated by a small number in the MLS Lead tab.</li><li>The new lead will appear in <strong>bold</strong> until you open it. If the lead is assigned to a staff member, it will be unbolded when the agent opens the lead.</li></ul><p><strong style="color: var(--p_color);">2. Automation</strong></p><ul><li><span style="color: var(--p_color);">The new lead will automatically be converted into a contact.</span></li><li>This contact will be saved with the appropriate category, such as &#8220;Estate Agent&#8221;.</li><li>The enquiry will be linked to both their contact and the property enquired about for easy access and management.</li></ul><p><strong>3.</strong> <strong style="color: var(--p_color);">Assigning a Staff Member to the New Lead</strong></p><ul><li>From this point, you can assign a staff member to manage the new lead.</li><li>If the contact already exists in the system:<br />&#8211; The contact will be updated with the property they have enquired about and their message.<br />&#8211; You will receive a notification in the same manner.</li></ul><p data-sourcepos="8:1-8:121">This streamlined system ensures you capture every opportunity and maximise your chances of converting leads into deals.</p><p data-sourcepos="8:1-8:121"><strong style="letter-spacing: 0.15px;"><a href="https://propertylist.es">PropertyList.es</a> – Your gateway to a thriving network of leads and partnerships!</strong></p>
`,
		},
		'sales-pipeline-tracking/generating-progress-reports': {
			title: 'Generating progress reports',
			desc: 'Create progress reports to track deals and update clients.',
			body: `
<h3 data-sourcepos="5:1-5:302">COMING SOON</h3><p data-sourcepos="5:1-5:302">Data is gold, but only if you can refine it into actionable insights. Generating reports is the process of transforming raw data from your CRM, sales funnel, or other sources into organised and digestible formats. These reports provide valuable summaries and visualizations of key metrics, helping you:</p><ul data-sourcepos="7:1-11:0"><li data-sourcepos="7:1-7:167"><strong>Track progress and identify trends:</strong> See how your sales pipeline is performing, monitor customer engagement levels, or analyse marketing campaign effectiveness.</li><li data-sourcepos="8:1-8:143"><strong>Make data-driven decisions:</strong> Use the insights gleaned from reports to guide your strategies, resource allocation, and marketing efforts.</li><li data-sourcepos="9:1-9:143"><strong>Improve performance:</strong> Identify areas for improvement and make adjustments to optimise your processes for greater efficiency and success.</li><li data-sourcepos="10:1-11:0"><strong>Share results with stakeholders:</strong> Generate clear and concise reports to keep your team, managers, or clients informed about progress and key performance indicators (KPIs).</li></ul><p data-sourcepos="12:1-12:221">Reports come in various formats, from basic tables and charts to sophisticated dashboards with interactive elements. Regardless of the format, generating reports empowers you to transform data into a strategic advantage.</p>
`,
		},
		'sales-pipeline-tracking/how-to-use-pipeline': {
			title: 'How to use Pipeline',
			desc: 'Move deals through stages and manage your sales workflow.',
			body: `
<p>All leads are automatically converted into contacts where you can <a href="https://info.propertylist.es/faq/how-can-i-assign-a-contact-to-a-specific-agent/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">assign a staff member</a> and add them to the pipeline.</p><h3>Building Strong Client Relationships</h3><p>Think of your client pipeline as a roadmap. By tracking your client pipeline, you can:</p><ul><li><p><strong>Identify Engagement Opportunities</strong>: Focus on nurturing relationships with potential clients.</p></li><li><p><strong>Prioritise High-Value Clients</strong>: Allocate resources effectively to prospects with the greatest potential.</p></li><li><p><strong>Optimise Client Onboarding</strong>: Ensure a smooth and positive experience for new clients.</p></li></ul><h3>Using The Client Pipeline:</h3><p><strong>Stages</strong>: PropertyList provides pre-defined stages in a colour-coded chart format:</p><ul><li><p><strong>Contacted</strong>: Initial point for all potential clients. Assign staff to the contact, and they will be notified of the new pipeline addition.</p></li><li><p><strong>Qualified</strong>: Verified as a viable lead, gathering detailed information about their requirements.</p></li><li><p><strong>Viewing</strong>: A property viewing has been confirmed or completed.</p></li><li><p><strong>Deposit Paid</strong>: Contact shows strong interest, signing and placing a reservation deposit.</p></li><li><p><strong>WON</strong>: Deal closed and property is under contract.</p></li><li><p><strong>LOST</strong>: Lead decided not to proceed. Dead lead.</p></li></ul><p>Find your “WON” and “LOST” leads in “Contact Pipeline- <strong>Table</strong>” &gt; “Stage” &gt; Select Won or Lost.</p><p>The chart visually displays the distribution of leads, highlighting where most are concentrated and potential bottlenecks.</p><p>You can edit the stage by clicking the pipeline contact or dragging it to another column.</p><div> </div><ul data-sourcepos="15:1-18:0"><li data-sourcepos="17:1-18:0"> </li></ul>
`,
		},
		'how-to-use-contacts/add-professional-contacts-to-a-contact': {
			title: 'Add professional contacts to a contact',
			desc: 'Attach relevant professionals (lawyer, mortgage broker, etc.) to a contact.',
			body: `
<p><strong>&#8211; COMING SOON</strong></p><ul><li data-sourcepos="3:1-3:226">Your CRM can be a powerful tool for managing your client relationships, and that includes keeping track of the professionals they work with. Here&#8217;s how to effortlessly link or add professional contacts to your client profiles with PropertyList.es:</li></ul><ol data-sourcepos="7:1-9:0"><li data-sourcepos="7:1-7:120"><strong>Access the Client Profile:</strong> Open the specific client&#8217;s profile you want to associate a professional contact with.</li><li data-sourcepos="8:1-9:0"><strong>Find the &#8220;Link Contact&#8221; Option:</strong> Look for a dedicated button labelled &#8220;Link Contact&#8221; within the client&#8217;s information page.</li></ol><p data-sourcepos="10:1-10:25"><strong>Adding a New Contact:</strong></p><ol data-sourcepos="12:1-14:0"><li data-sourcepos="12:1-12:225"><strong>Fill in the Details:</strong> Once you&#8217;ve selected &#8220;Link Contact,&#8221; you can enter the new professional&#8217;s information directly. This typically includes name, title, company affiliation, and contact details (email, phone number).</li><li data-sourcepos="13:1-14:0"><strong>Specify the Relationship:</strong> A key feature is the ability to define the type of professional contact. Choose from a list of options like &#8220;Lawyer,&#8221; &#8220;Architect,&#8221; &#8220;Gardener,&#8221; &#8220;Keyholder&#8221; and more. This helps categorize your client&#8217;s network for future reference.</li></ol><p data-sourcepos="15:1-15:34"><strong>Adding from Existing Professional Contacts:</strong></p><ol data-sourcepos="17:1-18:0"><li data-sourcepos="17:1-18:0"><strong>Select from Your List:</strong> If the professional contact already exists in your CRM, you can simply choose them from a dropdown menu instead of entering all the details again.</li></ol><p data-sourcepos="19:1-19:38"><strong>Benefits of Linking Professionals:</strong></p><ul data-sourcepos="21:1-24:0"><li data-sourcepos="21:1-21:140"><strong>Enhanced Client Service:</strong> By having all relevant professionals linked to a client, you can streamline communication and collaboration.</li><li data-sourcepos="22:1-22:141"><strong>Improved Organization:</strong> Categorize your client&#8217;s network for better searchability and reference, helping you understand their ecosystem.</li><li data-sourcepos="23:1-24:0"><strong>Streamlined Workflow:</strong> Easily access contact information for all parties involved with a client, saving time and effort.</li></ul>
`,
		},
		'how-to-use-contacts/adding-a-contact': {
			title: 'Adding a contact',
			desc: 'Create contacts and keep a clear contact history timeline.',
			body: `
<p data-sourcepos="3:1-3:113"><strong>Effortlessly expand your network!</strong> Adding new contacts to PropertyList.es is quick and convenient. Here&#8217;s how:</p><ol data-sourcepos="5:1-10:0"><li data-sourcepos="5:1-5:143"><strong>Navigate to &#8220;Contacts&#8221;:</strong> Locate the &#8220;CONTACTS&#8221; tab within your PropertyList.es account. </li><li data-sourcepos="6:1-6:120"><strong>Click &#8220;Add Contact&#8221;:</strong> Look for a button labelled &#8220;Create Contact&#8221;. This will open a contact creation form.</li><li data-sourcepos="7:1-7:146"><strong>Enter Details:</strong> Fill in the contact information fields, such as name, email address, phone number, and company affiliation (if applicable).</li><li data-sourcepos="8:1-8:173"><strong>Optional Information:</strong> Depending on your needs, you can add additional details like website, social media handles, or even a custom label to categorise your contacts.</li><li data-sourcepos="9:1-10:0"><strong>Save and Organise:</strong> Once all information is entered, click &#8220;Save&#8221;. Your new contact will be saved in your central contact list.</li></ol><p data-sourcepos="11:1-11:196"><strong>Bonus Tip: </strong>Leads are automatically converted into contacts. This can save you time by pre-populating some contact information and linking the enquiry with the contact. </p><p data-sourcepos="11:1-11:196"> </p><h3 data-sourcepos="3:1-3:144"><strong>Stay in the loop with complete contact history!</strong></h3><p data-sourcepos="3:1-3:144">PropertyList provides a dedicated timeline for each contact, giving you a clear view of:</p><ul data-sourcepos="5:1-7:0"><li data-sourcepos="5:1-5:89"><strong>All communication:</strong> See every enquiry or message sent and received, along with any links shared and more.</li><li data-sourcepos="6:1-7:0"><strong>Detailed edits:</strong> Track changes made to contact information, with timestamps and usernames for complete transparency.</li></ul><p data-sourcepos="8:1-8:99">This comprehensive timeline empowers you to stay informed and build stronger client relationships.</p><p data-sourcepos="13:1-13:146"> </p>
`,
		},
		'how-to-use-contacts/assign-contact-to-an-agent': {
			title: 'Assign contact to an agent',
			desc: 'Assign contacts to specific agents for clear ownership and follow-up.',
			body: `
<p data-sourcepos="3:1-3:230">Managing a large client base requires a well-oiled system. Assigning contacts to specific agents ensures clear communication, accountability, and a smoother experience for everyone. Here&#8217;s how to leverage this feature in your CRM:</p> <p data-sourcepos="5:1-5:26"><strong>Finding Your Contacts:</strong></p> <ol data-sourcepos="7:1-9:0"> <li data-sourcepos="7:1-7:92"><strong>Navigate to the &#8220;CONTACTS&#8221; tab.</strong>&nbsp;This is your central hub for all client information.</li> <li data-sourcepos="8:1-9:0"><strong>Search or Filter:</strong>&nbsp;Easily find the specific contact you need by searching their name, or use filters to refine your search based on stages, sources, buyer/landlord status, and other criteria.</li> </ol> <p data-sourcepos="10:1-10:30"><strong>Assigning the Right Agent:</strong></p> <ol data-sourcepos="12:1-16:0"> <li data-sourcepos="12:1-12:83"><strong>Open the Contact:</strong>&nbsp;Click on the specific client&#8217;s profile you want to assign.</li> <li data-sourcepos="13:1-13:139"><strong>Edit and Find Assignment:</strong>&nbsp;Locate the &#8220;EDIT&#8221; button and access the &#8220;ASSIGN AGENT&#8221; button.</li> <li data-sourcepos="14:1-14:231"><strong>Choose Your Team:</strong>&nbsp;A list of all your agents will appear. Select the most suitable agent based on expertise, workload, or existing relationships with the client. You can even assign multiple agents for collaborative efforts.</li> <li data-sourcepos="15:1-16:0"><strong>Save and Notify:</strong>&nbsp;Finalize the process by saving the contact information. The assigned agent(s) will automatically receive a notification about their new client.</li> </ol> <p data-sourcepos="17:1-17:35"><strong>Benefits of Assigning Contacts:</strong></p> <ul data-sourcepos="19:1-22:0"> <li data-sourcepos="19:1-19:122"><strong>Enhanced Teamwork:</strong>&nbsp;Agents focus on their assigned clients, fostering better communication and personalized service.</li> <li data-sourcepos="20:1-20:101"><strong>Boosted Efficiency:</strong>&nbsp;Clear ownership avoids confusion and ensures tasks are completed promptly.</li> <li data-sourcepos="21:1-22:0"><strong>Streamlined Workflows:</strong>&nbsp;Agents have easy access to relevant client information and can track progress on their assigned tasks.</li> </ul>
`,
		},
		'how-to-use-contacts/link-documents-to-a-contact': {
			title: 'Link/add documents to a contact',
			desc: 'Attach documents to contacts and properties to keep records organised.',
			body: `
<p><strong>Keeping Your Records Organised: Attaching Documents to Contacts and Properties</strong></p><p data-sourcepos="3:1-3:158">Staying organised requires keeping all relevant information together. Here&#8217;s how to effortlessly attach documents to both contacts and properties in your CRM:</p><p data-sourcepos="5:1-5:26"><strong>Attaching to Contacts:</strong></p><ol data-sourcepos="7:1-9:0"><li data-sourcepos="7:1-7:168"><strong>Access the Contact:</strong> Locate the specific contact you want to associate a document with. </li><li data-sourcepos="7:1-7:168"><strong style="text-align: var(--text-align); color: var(--p_color); letter-spacing: 0.15px;">Find the Section:</strong><span style="text-align: var(--text-align); color: var(--p_color); letter-spacing: 0.15px;"> Look for a dedicated section labelled &#8220;Attached Documents,&#8221; within the contact&#8217;s information page.</span></li></ol><p data-sourcepos="10:1-10:28"><strong>Attaching to Properties:</strong></p><ol data-sourcepos="12:1-15:0"><li data-sourcepos="12:1-12:153"><strong>Edit the Property:</strong> Find the specific property you want to link a document to. Click on the &#8220;Edit&#8221; button or option associated with the property.</li><li data-sourcepos="13:1-13:128"><strong>Navigate to Admin Section:</strong> Within the edit options, locate a section titled &#8220;Admin&#8221;.</li><li data-sourcepos="14:1-15:0"><strong>Find the Attachment Feature:</strong> Look for a button labelled &#8220;Attach New Document&#8221; within the admin section.</li></ol><p data-sourcepos="16:1-16:36"><strong>Benefits of Attaching Documents:</strong></p><ul data-sourcepos="18:1-21:0"><li data-sourcepos="18:1-18:127"><strong>Centralised Information:</strong> Keep all relevant documents related to a contact or property readily accessible in one location.</li><li data-sourcepos="19:1-19:117"><strong>Improved Context:</strong> Documents provide valuable context and details, enhancing communication and decision-making.</li><li data-sourcepos="20:1-21:0"><strong>Streamlined Workflow:</strong> Eliminate the need to search for documents scattered across different locations.</li></ul><p><a href="https://info.propertylist.es/docs/propertylist-mls-user-manual/documents/share-documents/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Find out how to share your document easily here.</a></p><p> </p><p><strong>PLEAE NOTE</strong>: <br />PropertyList<strong> does not have access</strong> to any contacts, property documents, or pipeline info. This ensures that your information remains secure within your office. <strong>However, please be careful when deleting any items, as we are unable to retrieve deleted information either.</strong></p>
`,
		},
		'how-to-use-contacts/link-properties-to-contact': {
			title: 'Link/add properties to a contact',
			desc: 'Link properties to contacts to centralise ownership and communication.',
			body: `
<p data-sourcepos="3:1-3:244">By linking properties to owners, you create a powerful information network that boosts your productivity and saves you time. Here&#8217;s how it works:</p><p data-sourcepos="5:1-5:21"><strong>Two Ways to Link:</strong></p><ol data-sourcepos="7:1-9:0"><li data-sourcepos="7:1-7:191"><strong>Link from Contact:</strong> Find the contact you&#8217;re working with and locate the &#8220;Link a Property&#8221; button. Choose the property you want to associate with them.</li><li data-sourcepos="8:1-9:0"><strong>Link from Property:</strong> Locate the specific property and look for the &#8220;EDIT&#8221; button. Under the &#8220;CONTACTS&#8221; tab, select &#8220;Add Owner&#8221; and add or create the relevant contact from the options.</li></ol><p data-sourcepos="14:1-14:24"><strong>Benefits of Linking:</strong></p><ul data-sourcepos="16:1-19:0"><li data-sourcepos="16:1-16:128"><strong>Effortless Organisation:</strong> No more juggling information across different sources. Everything&#8217;s centralised for easy access.</li><li data-sourcepos="17:1-17:121"><strong>Streamlined Workflow:</strong> Automated updates based on contact status save you valuable time and keep your data accurate.</li><li data-sourcepos="18:1-19:0"><strong>Personalised Communication:</strong> Access linked property information to tailor your interactions with each contact.</li></ul><p> </p><p><strong>PLEAE NOTE</strong>: <br />PropertyList<strong> does not have access</strong> to any contacts, property documents, or pipeline info. This ensures that your information remains secure within your office. <strong>However, please be careful when deleting any items, as we are unable to retrieve deleted information either.</strong></p>
`,
