		'how-to-use-the-calendar/managing-your-schedule-and-tasks': {
			title: 'Managing your schedule and tasks',
			desc: 'Create events, link contacts and properties, and set reminders.',
			body: `
<p>Managing your schedule effectively is crucial, especially when dealing with real estate. Let’s break down the steps for managing your schedule on PropertyList:</p><p><strong>Access the Calendar:</strong></p><ul><li><span style="color: var(--p_color);">Log in to your PropertyList.es account.</span></li><li>On the left-hand side, click the “Calendar” tab. This will take you to your calendar view.</li></ul><p><strong>Create a New Event:</strong><strong><br /></strong><span style="color: var(--p_color);">Once you’re in the calendar view, you have two options</span></p><ul><li><strong>Option A: Click New Event<br /></strong>Look for a button or link that says “New Event”. Click it.</li><li><strong>Option B: Select a Time Slot<br /></strong>Alternatively, you can click directly on the desired time slot on the calendar where you want to schedule an event.</li></ul><p><strong style="color: var(--p_color);">Event Details:</strong></p><p>You’ll now be prompted to provide details for the event:</p><p><strong>Event Title:<br /></strong>Make it descriptive so you can easily identify the event later.</p><ul><li><strong>Start and End Time:<br /></strong>Specify the start and end time for the event. If it’s an all-day event, mark it as such.</li><li><strong>Event Note:<br /></strong>Write any relevant notes about the event.</li><li><strong>Agents:<br /></strong>Assign the agent(s) who should be linked to this event. Each agent you select will receive notifications related to this event.</li><li><strong>Notifications:<br /></strong>Decide when you want to be notified about this event (e.g., 15 minutes before, 1 hour before).</li><li><strong>Add Property:<br /></strong>If the event is related to a specific property from the MLS, add it here.</li><li><strong>Add Contact:<br /></strong>Link the event to a saved contact (e.g., client, buyer, seller).</li></ul><p><strong style="color: var(--p_color);">Save the Event:</strong></p><ul><li>Once you’ve filled in all the necessary details, look for a “Save” button.</li><li>Click “Save” to add the event to your calendar.</li></ul><p> </p><p><span style="color: var(--p_color);"><strong>Remember!</strong> Keeping your calendar organised and up-to-date is essential for successful real estate management. If you have any other questions or need further assistance, feel free to ask!</span></p><p> </p><p><em><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong>Note:</strong></span> The instructions here are based on general principles for managing schedules and events. Specific steps may vary slightly depending on the exact interface and features of <a role="link" href="https://propertylist.es/?form=MG0AV3" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="https://PropertyList.es">PropertyList.es </a>in future updates. We strive to keep this information as current as possible. If you notice any discrepancies, please inform <a href="https://info.propertylist.es/docs/propertylist-mls-user-manual/additional-resources/mls-support/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">support.</a></em></p>
`,
		},
		'security/complying-with-data-protection-regulations': {
			title: 'Complying with Data Protection Regulations',
			desc: 'Learn about GDPR-aligned practices and how data is handled.',
			body: `
<h3><strong>Our Commitment to Your Privacy</strong></h3><p>At PropertyList.es, we are dedicated to ensuring that your personal and property information is handled with the utmost care and in full compliance with data protection regulations.</p><p><strong>Our Compliance Measures:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Adherence to GDPR:</strong> We strictly follow the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR), which sets the standard for data protection and privacy in the European Union.</li><li><strong>Data Protection Act 2018:</strong> As part of our commitment, we comply with the UK’s Data Protection Act 2018, which complements GDPR and provides additional safeguards for your data.</li><li><strong>Transparent Data Practices:</strong> We ensure that your data is processed fairly, lawfully, and transparently. We only collect and use data for specified, explicit purposes.</li><li><strong>Data Minimisation:</strong> We adhere to the principle of data minimisation, ensuring that we only collect data that is adequate, relevant, and limited to what is necessary for our services.</li><li><strong>User Rights:</strong> We respect your rights under data protection laws, including the right to access, update, erase, or object to the processing of your personal data.</li><li><strong>Regular Audits and Assessments:</strong> We conduct regular audits and assessments to ensure our data protection practices are up to date and in line with regulatory requirements.</li></ul><p>By implementing these comprehensive measures, we ensure that your data is protected and your privacy is respected. At PropertyList.es, your trust is our priority, and we are committed to maintaining a secure and compliant environment for all our users.</p><p> </p><p><strong>PLEAE NOTE</strong>: <br />PropertyList<strong> does not have access</strong> to any contacts, property documents, or pipeline info. This ensures that your information remains secure within your office. <strong>However, please be careful when deleting any items, as we are unable to retrieve deleted information either.</strong></p>
`,
		},
		'security/incident-response': {
			title: 'Incident Response',
			desc: 'How PropertyList responds to and recovers from security incidents.',
			body: `
<p>At PropertyList.es, we are committed to maintaining the highest standards of security. In the unlikely event of a security incident, we have a robust incident response plan in place to ensure swift and effective action.</p><p><strong>Our Incident Response Measures:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Immediate Detection and Analysis:</strong> Our security team continuously monitors our systems to detect any suspicious activity. Upon identifying a potential incident, we promptly analyse the situation to understand its scope and impact.</li><li><strong>Containment and Mitigation:</strong> We take immediate steps to contain the incident and mitigate any potential damage. This includes isolating affected systems and implementing measures to prevent further unauthorised access.</li><li><strong>Eradication and Recovery:</strong> Once the incident is contained, we work diligently to eradicate the root cause and restore affected systems to normal operation. Our goal is to ensure minimal disruption to our services.</li><li><strong>Communication and Reporting:</strong> We maintain transparent communication with our users and relevant authorities throughout the incident response process. We keep timely updates and detailed reports for internal use.</li><li><strong>Post-Incident Review:</strong> After resolving the incident, we conduct a thorough review to identify lessons learned and improve our security measures. This helps us enhance our defences and prevent future incidents.</li></ul><p>With these comprehensive incident response measures, you can trust that PropertyList.es is prepared to handle any security challenges effectively. Your safety and security are our top priorities, and we are dedicated to maintaining a secure environment for all our users.</p>
`,
		},
